---
// Renewable-energy and carbon-removal note (Q-VS-33, John 2026-11-24).
// Cloudflare claim checked 2026-11-24: 100% renewable by annual matching, not zero impact.
interface Props {
  class?: string;
}
const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<p class:list={['flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed max-w-3xl', className]}>
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
    width="20"
    height="20"
    fill="none"
    stroke="currentColor"
    stroke-width="1.75"
    stroke-linecap="round"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
    class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[var(--color-good-foreground)]"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
    <path d="M2 12h20"></path>
    <path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"
    ></path>
  </svg>
  <span>
    My own servers have run on wind and hydro power since 2001. The sites I build are hosted on <a
      href="https://www.cloudflare.com/impact/"
      class="underline underline-offset-4 text-foreground">Cloudflare</a
    >, which buys renewable energy to match all the electricity its network uses each year. And
    0.5% of every payment to Vashon Software goes to carbon removal through <a
      href="https://climate.stripe.com/"
      class="underline underline-offset-4 text-foreground">Stripe Climate</a
    >.
  </span>
</p>
